==> demo-2: per-stack Directus + cache-first snapshot replay (taxonomy + directus + sim-embeddings)
per-stack Directus provision recipe for demo-2 (M10 store fork — bootstrap → content-schema → replay → boot):
  1. bootstrap-system-schema Directus creates its OWN directus_* SYSTEM tables (27 of them — and nothing else; the content tables come from the content-schema step below). The schema must exist first and bootstrap must be pointed at it via DB_SEARCH_PATH=directus, else everything lands in `public`. The image entrypoint runs `node <arg>`, so the subcommand is `node cli.js bootstrap` (a bare `bootstrap` arg dies MODULE_NOT_FOUND). Two DSNs: psql runs on the HOST (the localhost offset-port DSN, inlined); the docker leg's $DEMO_2_DIRECTUS_DSN must be CONTAINER-reachable (host.docker.internal:25432 on Docker Desktop, or the stack's compose network + service name) — one value cannot serve both sides. ADMIN_TOKEN sets a LOCALLY-MINTED static token on the bootstrapped admin (M23): studio-desk uses it as DIRECTUS_TOKEN so its skill-path WRITES target THIS per-stack Directus, never prod.
     $ psql "postgres://postgres@localhost:25432/postgres" -c 'CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS directus' && docker run --rm -e DB_CLIENT=pg -e DB_CONNECTION_STRING=$DEMO_2_DIRECTUS_DSN -e DB_SEARCH_PATH=directus -e SECRET=local-directus-secret-demo_2 -e ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@demo-2.example.com -e ADMIN_PASSWORD=local-directus-demo_2 -e ADMIN_TOKEN=local-directus-token-demo_2 directus/directus:11.6.1 node cli.js bootstrap
  2. content-schema          Create the user-collection table STRUCTURE (the 26 collections' DDL + PRIMARY KEYs) in the directus schema so the schema digest converges to the captured source (M21 option A). AUTOMATED (M21): the next `stacksnap replay` step AUTO-PROVISIONS this from the snapshot's Structure artifact — on a bootstrapped-gap directus schema (digest miss), replay applies the captured structure, re-probes, then loads. No separate command. (The snapshot must be a structure-bearing capture — re-capture once per release if the cache predates the M21 structure extension.) NOTE: collection REGISTRATION (directus_collections) + the public READ permissions a booted Directus needs to SERVE are the M21 serve-rows piece (in progress) — until they land, the schema + rows are correct but anonymous serving needs the hand recipe (corpus/ops/snapshot-spec.md).
     $ # AUTOMATED by the next replay step (M21 structure auto-provision) — no separate command
  3. replay-content          AUTO-PROVISION the table structure (if the directus schema is bootstrapped-gap) THEN bulk-COPY the captured public content rows (304 sims / 22 paths / children) into the user-collection tables in the stack's directus schema. Per-stack-isolated → the seeding guard allows it (class postgres). Exits 0 on success; exit 4 if the directus schema is missing (bootstrap first); exit 5 only on a genuine cache miss / unmigrated divergence.
     $ stacksnap replay --surface directus --stack demo-2
  4. boot-directus           Boot the per-stack Directus container pointed at the stack's directus schema (same DB_SEARCH_PATH), published on the stack's offset port. CMS + studio-desk for this stack point their DIRECTUS_BASE_ADDR at THIS container (the offset port), not content.anthropos.work.
     $ docker run -d --name demo-2-directus -p 28055:8055 -e DB_CLIENT=pg -e DB_CONNECTION_STRING=$DEMO_2_DIRECTUS_DSN -e DB_SEARCH_PATH=directus -e SECRET=local-directus-secret-demo_2 directus/directus:11.6.1

